# Test: with no ze running, an external plugin's command typed in the shell is not available
#
# Question: with no ze running and a stored config that declares an external
# plugin, does `ze show <the plugin's command>`, a path the ze binary's
# compiled-in command tree does not hold, refuse with exit 1, say the command
# is not available and may belong to an external plugin that only a running ze
# holds, say why no ze answered, and name the one fix `ze start`, without
# starting the plugin's program?
# Why not a unit test: TestUnheldPathNoZeExternalPluginDeclared
# (cmd/ze/internal/cmdutil/unheld_test.go) proves the wording over a stubbed
# walk and a stubbed config. Only the real command shows the walk to the
# daemon's listener failing, the stored config being read for its plugin
# declarations, and no program being started.
#
# The program the config declares writes a marker when it is started, then
# runs the `commands` variant of the fixture plugin, so a command that ran it
# leaves the marker behind.
#
# The config is put in the store (`ze config import`): with no argument, the
# stored config is the one a bare `ze start` boots, so it is the config whose
# plugins could answer the command. It declares the plugin and no section of
# it, so nothing in this test depends on parsing an external plugin's schema.
# The store lives on disk (option=storage:value=disk): the store the fixture
# seeds, the one `ze config import` writes and the one each `ze show` reads
# are then the same store under the work directory, where the default
# in-memory store would die with each process.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-plugin-external-yang-at-startup AC-37, under the owner ruling
#   of 2026-11-16: with no daemon running, what needs an external plugin is
#   not available, and the refusal says what is true and names one fix.
# PREVENTS: "unknown command" for a command the plugin serves once ze runs; a
#   program started with no daemon.

option=timeout:value=60s
option=storage:value=disk
option=env:var=ze.config.dir:value=.
option=env:var=ze.ssh.username:value=admin
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass
option=env:var=ze.ssh.port:value=$PORT

tmpfs=marker.run:terminator=EOF_RUN
echo started > started-by-ze.marker
exec le test fixture plugin/external-yang commands
EOF_RUN

tmpfs=ze.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
bus {
	endpoint acme-monitor {
		external {
			run "sh marker.run";
		}
		encoding json;
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture storage/empty-tree:exit=0
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config import ze.conf:exit=0

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze show acme-monitor status:exit=1
expect=stderr:contains=error: show acme-monitor status is not available
expect=stderr:contains=it may belong to an external plugin, which only a running ze holds
expect=stderr:contains=the config declares external plugin "acme-monitor"
expect=stderr:contains=No running ze answered: no ze listens at 127.0.0.1:
expect=stderr:contains=then `ze show acme-monitor status` again
expect=stderr:contains=fix: ze start
reject=stderr:contains=unknown command

cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze show acme-monitor target probe-b:exit=1
expect=stderr:contains=error: show acme-monitor target probe-b is not available
expect=stderr:contains=fix: ze start
reject=stderr:contains=unknown command

cmd=foreground:seq=5:exec=ze show acme-monitor status:exit=1
expect=file:path=started-by-ze.marker:absent=true
